  "title": "Carlos Finlay",
  "summary": "Carlos Juan Finlay was born in Puerto Príncipe (today Camagüey), Cuba, in 1833 and died in 1915. On 14 August 1881 he presented a paper to the Royal Academy in Havana proposing that the mosquito carried yellow fever; it was largely dismissed, and the Walter Reed Commission of 1900 proved the idea.",
